WEBVTT

00:06.506 --> 00:09.092
[sweet airy music]

00:47.172 --> 00:49.299
[Ji-ung] Every life is
in itself a work of art.

00:50.884 --> 00:53.136
[gentle music]

00:58.141 --> 00:59.934
[gasps, sighs]

01:01.478 --> 01:04.898
And it becomes complete
only when all the pieces are collected.

01:07.317 --> 01:09.486
[gentle music continues]

01:09.569 --> 01:10.987
[door opening]

01:11.071 --> 01:13.114
- [gasps]
- [door closes]

01:18.036 --> 01:19.788
Hey, you should be in bed.

01:22.749 --> 01:25.502
[gentle music]

01:28.129 --> 01:29.380
[young Ji-ung] Hey, Mom.

01:29.464 --> 01:32.675
You wanna know what happened?
I made a new friend today,

01:32.759 --> 01:35.762
- and he has the same name as mine.
- Look, I'm really tired.

01:40.558 --> 01:42.227
[sighs]

01:43.645 --> 01:46.564
I told you to sleep first
because I was coming home late.

01:54.781 --> 01:57.117
[Ji-ung] But I think my life
can't be complete

01:58.451 --> 02:01.079
because of a piece
that I've never had before.

02:02.330 --> 02:05.333
[soft emotional music]

02:08.711 --> 02:09.754
[inhales]

02:13.633 --> 02:14.884
[groans]

02:24.894 --> 02:27.188
[soft emotional music continues]

02:42.078 --> 02:44.706
[soft emotional music]

02:48.042 --> 02:49.836
I didn't understand the reason.

02:49.919 --> 02:52.380
Now you listen to your teacher, okay?

02:53.131 --> 02:55.425
Let's go!
[chuckles]

02:55.508 --> 02:56.634
Hey!

02:56.718 --> 02:59.220
Mom, that's my friend! His name is Ji-ung.

02:59.304 --> 03:02.473
Oh, hello! So are you Ji-ung?

03:02.557 --> 03:04.684
It's nice to meet you. I'm Ung's mother.

03:04.767 --> 03:07.061
- [Ji-ung] It was a piece everyone had…
- Nice to meet you.

03:07.645 --> 03:09.480
You're a bright looking kid.
[chuckles]

03:11.024 --> 03:13.651
[Yeon-ok] Thank you so much
for being Ung's friend, all right.

03:15.028 --> 03:17.864
- [Ji-ung] …it wasn't so hard to have.
- Go to school with your friend, all right?

03:17.947 --> 03:20.992
[Ji-ung] I just didn't know
why I didn't have it too.

03:24.078 --> 03:25.371
[delivery man] All right.

03:25.455 --> 03:26.581
Hm.
[inhales]

03:26.664 --> 03:27.999
[sighs]

03:30.335 --> 03:31.210
Here.

03:32.253 --> 03:33.463
Are you eating alone again?

03:37.050 --> 03:39.802
Here you go. Put the bowl outside
when you're done.

03:40.345 --> 03:43.389
[Ji-ung] The memories I have
of my childhood days…

03:43.473 --> 03:45.433
- [delivery man sighs]
- [door squeaks]

03:46.059 --> 03:47.060
…are of being alone…

03:49.854 --> 03:52.065
[gentle music]

03:59.405 --> 04:01.324
…or being with a friend who was alone.

04:03.993 --> 04:04.994
[chomps]

04:08.414 --> 04:12.627
And being with her
for just a handful of moments.

04:15.380 --> 04:17.423
[gentle music continues]

04:24.430 --> 04:25.640
And that was it.

04:28.351 --> 04:29.560
And when time passed…

04:31.688 --> 04:34.065
and I grew old enough
to remember everything,

04:38.111 --> 04:39.487
[sighs]

04:41.781 --> 04:43.741
[gentle music]

04:43.825 --> 04:46.119
[slurping]

04:48.705 --> 04:51.249
- I felt numb to a lot of things.
- [slurps]

04:54.460 --> 04:55.753
But that doesn't mean

04:57.171 --> 04:59.007
that I got used to everything right away.

05:01.592 --> 05:02.677
And around that time…

05:04.345 --> 05:05.638
You don't have a dad either?

05:05.722 --> 05:07.932
No. And you? You don't either?

05:10.184 --> 05:11.644
So do you live with your mom?

05:11.728 --> 05:12.854
Hmm.

05:13.688 --> 05:15.273
It must be tough, huh?

05:15.356 --> 05:18.943
Nah. Why would it be tough for me?
My mom's the one who suffered.

05:19.027 --> 05:20.903
She had a fever last night too,

05:20.987 --> 05:23.114
so I told her not to go to work today.

05:23.197 --> 05:24.824
[teenager] But she never listens to me.

05:24.907 --> 05:27.452
She makes a huge fuss
whenever I get sick, though.

05:27.535 --> 05:28.411
[scoffs]

05:28.494 --> 05:30.038
I guess that you two must be close.

05:30.121 --> 05:32.707
How can we not be?
We have to stick together.

05:33.833 --> 05:37.337
Anyway, hey, I told our teacher
I'd be leaving early,

05:37.420 --> 05:39.005
so please tell the others for me.

05:40.631 --> 05:42.759
But we have exams tomorrow,
are you gonna be okay?

05:42.842 --> 05:45.887
My mom's gonna yell at me
if she finds out I went home early,

05:45.970 --> 05:47.722
but I know she'll be fine with it.

05:47.805 --> 05:49.557
She can't live without me, you know.

05:49.640 --> 05:50.641
Hm.

05:50.725 --> 05:52.310
- I'm going.
- Hmm.

05:54.604 --> 05:56.272
[Ji-ung] So I got curious.

05:57.940 --> 06:00.276
And I wanted to figure out the reason why…

06:01.527 --> 06:03.196
I couldn't have that piece.

06:06.199 --> 06:08.493
[vulnerable music]

06:21.380 --> 06:22.507
[music fades]

06:38.773 --> 06:40.608
Hey, Mom, do you think…

06:47.615 --> 06:49.784
Do you think that
you could live without me?

07:00.002 --> 07:01.003
[bottle thuds]

07:04.882 --> 07:06.592
Why are we living like this?

07:08.678 --> 07:11.639
Why do you and I have to pretend
like we hate each other--

07:11.722 --> 07:12.849
If you weren't here…

07:14.934 --> 07:17.019
I wouldn't be living like this.

07:19.272 --> 07:21.774
[emotional music]

07:24.986 --> 07:26.529
Without you…

07:29.323 --> 07:30.575
I wouldn't be living…

07:32.577 --> 07:34.787
such a pathetic life like this.

07:38.624 --> 07:41.627
[Ji-ung] Oh, that's when I realized…

07:42.712 --> 07:46.674
I was the useless piece.
I couldn't fit in her life.

07:48.301 --> 07:50.011
The thing I wanted so desperately

07:51.512 --> 07:53.806
was something that ruined her life.

08:00.104 --> 08:04.484
So I decided that I would never
have that piece no matter what.

08:05.568 --> 08:07.653
My life was never a work of art.

08:09.363 --> 08:10.740
It was just an episode

08:11.699 --> 08:15.995
of a boring documentary
that no one would ever care to watch.

08:16.078 --> 08:19.123
EPISODE 15
THREE IDIOTS

08:23.794 --> 08:26.964
Hmm, I just went to the gallery
to check up on something.

08:27.048 --> 08:28.466
But I am heading back now.

08:29.717 --> 08:31.385
Go inside and get some rest.

08:31.469 --> 08:33.179
I'll be home soon. It's so cold.

08:33.262 --> 08:34.180
Mm-hmm.

08:34.722 --> 08:35.806
[phone chimes]

08:48.486 --> 08:50.363
Let's just not
give each other presents, okay?

08:50.446 --> 08:52.823
The culture of giving gifts
is just a marketing ploy

08:52.907 --> 08:54.325
to make people spend a lot.

08:54.408 --> 08:55.701
Love is what's important.

08:55.785 --> 08:58.246
And I think spending money
on gifts is just meaningless.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.332
[Yeon-su] But back then,

09:01.415 --> 09:05.378
I only said all that to you because
I didn't want to take up your time.

09:06.587 --> 09:08.673
You didn't want me to come see you?

09:08.756 --> 09:09.799
[Yeon-su] Hmm.

09:09.882 --> 09:11.217
[car honking]

09:14.136 --> 09:16.264
[light music]

09:19.350 --> 09:20.560
May I help you, sir?

09:20.643 --> 09:21.602
[Ung] Oh, yeah.

09:21.686 --> 09:24.105
[retailer] Are you buying a gift?
Is it for your girlfriend?

09:24.647 --> 09:25.898
Yes, for my girlfriend.

09:25.982 --> 09:29.443
I see. What kind of style
would you say your girlfriend prefers?

09:30.236 --> 09:32.863
Well, she's, she's really pretty.

09:33.614 --> 09:35.074
Oh…
[chuckles]

09:35.157 --> 09:39.328
What I mean is, what kind of outfits
or accessories does she usually wear?

09:39.412 --> 09:42.373
Oh! Oh, okay. Uh…

09:42.456 --> 09:45.084
She's neat and tidy,
you could say, I guess.

09:45.167 --> 09:47.169
[retailer] I see. Neat and tidy then, huh?

09:53.926 --> 09:54.885
[hums in thought]

09:55.469 --> 09:56.304
[gasps]

10:00.308 --> 10:02.727
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

10:20.328 --> 10:22.455
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim continues]

10:33.674 --> 10:34.884
What's that?

10:36.302 --> 10:38.304
I'm just putting a bell on a cat.

10:39.555 --> 10:40.431
[chuckles]

10:47.855 --> 10:48.773
[Ung groans]

10:53.527 --> 10:54.820
[Ung chuckles]

10:54.904 --> 10:57.531
On my way home,
I saw the store having a huge sale.

10:57.615 --> 10:58.991
They said I couldn't afford to miss it.

10:59.784 --> 11:02.995
And I thought it would look better on you
than it would on me.

11:04.497 --> 11:05.456
It's really pretty.

11:06.290 --> 11:07.124
What?

11:08.334 --> 11:09.460
Thank you.

11:11.420 --> 11:14.715
I got it at full price.
It took me an hour to choose.

11:14.799 --> 11:16.050
Oh.

11:17.134 --> 11:18.844
- I got you earrings too.
- [Yeon-su chuckles]

11:18.928 --> 11:19.804
Here, try them on.

11:19.887 --> 11:21.514
[chuckles]

11:22.098 --> 11:24.392
["Summer Rain" continuing]

11:31.232 --> 11:32.233
[chuckles]

11:35.111 --> 11:37.488
- So do you like them?
- Mm-hmm.

11:39.407 --> 11:40.658
Oh.

11:41.158 --> 11:42.493
[Yeon-su] What do you say if we

11:42.576 --> 11:45.371
hang out at home all day
instead of going out?

11:45.996 --> 11:47.206
Hmm.

11:48.916 --> 11:51.168
You know that's what I'm best at.

11:51.252 --> 11:52.753
[chuckles]

11:52.837 --> 11:54.880
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

11:56.257 --> 12:00.010
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT'S DREAM

12:02.763 --> 12:04.765
- Are you done reading?
- Mm-hmm.

12:07.601 --> 12:11.188
♪ When the rain stops ♪

12:11.272 --> 12:14.358
♪ You shine on me ♪

12:14.859 --> 12:16.694
♪ Your light's the only thing… ♪

12:16.777 --> 12:19.905
[Yeon-su] What? Why did you make so much?

12:20.781 --> 12:22.616
That's right. I made more than I thought.

12:22.700 --> 12:24.827
How are we going to eat all this?

12:24.910 --> 12:26.454
Well, I think we can eat it all.

12:26.537 --> 12:28.539
- It looks good, right?
- Mm-hmm.

12:29.331 --> 12:30.583
[Yeon-su] It does look tasty.

12:31.417 --> 12:32.585
I'm so full.

12:33.210 --> 12:35.754
- [Ung] Me too. I'm so full.
- [Yeon-su] Look at me.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.590
- Look at my tummy.
- [chuckles]

12:38.757 --> 12:40.384
- Are you feeling okay?
- Yeah.

12:40.468 --> 12:42.178
Who's in charge of the dishes?

12:42.261 --> 12:43.762
[both] Rock, paper, scissors.

12:44.472 --> 12:48.100
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

12:48.767 --> 12:50.895
I'm not done drawing yet.

12:50.978 --> 12:54.315
♪ A million little reasons ♪

12:54.398 --> 12:57.735
♪ I'm falling for your eyes ♪

12:58.319 --> 12:59.195
[Ung] Are you done?

12:59.278 --> 13:02.865
♪ I just want to be where you are ♪

13:05.910 --> 13:07.328
One, two, three.

13:08.954 --> 13:10.581
[laughs]

13:11.248 --> 13:12.416
What's so funny?

13:13.959 --> 13:17.129
You made Jjongjjong look so ugly in yours!

13:17.213 --> 13:20.925
No, I didn't I think I made him
super cute! Look at him.

13:21.008 --> 13:22.676
[Ung laughs loudly]

13:23.677 --> 13:25.012
[Yeon-su] Hey!

13:26.347 --> 13:27.640
[laughs]

13:28.557 --> 13:29.642
Hey!

13:29.725 --> 13:30.851
[Yeon-su] Screw you!

13:30.935 --> 13:32.645
Hey, these are expensive!

13:33.604 --> 13:35.773
[Ung groaning]
Darn it.

13:36.398 --> 13:39.693
- ["Christmas Tree" continuing]
- [indistinct TV chatter]

13:41.362 --> 13:43.322
[Ung] Can we not
watch a documentary tonight?

13:43.405 --> 13:45.783
Why not?
I really wanted to watch this one.

13:45.866 --> 13:47.076
Aren't you sick of them?

13:47.952 --> 13:50.037
[financial documentary playing on TV]

13:51.497 --> 13:53.999
- What do you wanna watch?
- Let's see what's on.

13:55.584 --> 13:56.961
Oh, that one!

13:58.420 --> 14:00.673
["Christmas Tree" continuing]

14:05.427 --> 14:06.345
[soft chuckle]

14:16.313 --> 14:17.481
SHOP FOR LUXURY ITEMS ON
TREN:BE

14:17.565 --> 14:20.192
HOT ITEMS THIS WINTER

14:22.653 --> 14:24.446
[sighs]
It sure is cold nowadays.

14:25.155 --> 14:26.574
[Ung] I should get a scarf.

14:27.366 --> 14:28.701
Oh, this one.

14:29.285 --> 14:30.661
[door opens]

14:30.744 --> 14:31.829
BUY NOW, SHOPPING CART

14:34.248 --> 14:35.958
- [Yeon-su] What are you doing?
- What?

14:37.459 --> 14:38.627
Oh, it's nothing.

14:39.837 --> 14:41.088
[sighs]

14:41.171 --> 14:44.758
You know, come to think of it,
you took a shower here last time too.

14:45.509 --> 14:46.927
It's still a guy's house.

14:47.011 --> 14:48.679
So what if I did? It's your house.

14:48.762 --> 14:50.556
But we weren't even dating back then.

14:52.099 --> 14:53.976
That's an enthusiastic greeting.

14:54.059 --> 14:57.396
Oh, when you said we'd just be friends?

14:57.479 --> 15:00.941
You… you don't do that
at all of your friends' homes, do you?

15:02.318 --> 15:04.069
- Why aren't you answering me?
- [inhales]

15:04.153 --> 15:06.280
I only did that to seduce you.

15:09.408 --> 15:11.702
- You're like a cunning desert fox.
- [scoffs]

15:11.785 --> 15:14.705
Hey, it's not "cunning desert fox,"
it's just "cunning fox."

15:14.788 --> 15:16.332
It's oddly offensive.

15:16.916 --> 15:18.918
- You sure have changed, Yeon-su.
- [chuckles]

15:19.001 --> 15:22.129
- Hey, dry my hair for me.
- What?

15:22.838 --> 15:23.881
I said, dry my hair.

15:23.964 --> 15:27.635
Come on, can't you even dry your own hair?
Why are you making me do it?

15:27.718 --> 15:29.011
You're unbelievable.

15:29.094 --> 15:30.471
[both chuckle]

15:30.971 --> 15:33.682
[sweet gentle music]

15:38.687 --> 15:41.398
All right, your hair is all dried
and ready now, ma'am.

15:41.482 --> 15:44.610
Thank you very much.
My right ear feel really hot, though.

15:44.693 --> 15:46.570
- But your hair is perfectly dry.
- [chuckles]

15:47.279 --> 15:49.990
Hey, are you going to keep asking me
to do this for you?

15:50.074 --> 15:51.116
[groans]

15:51.909 --> 15:53.994
Please do. Keep doing it for me.

15:54.078 --> 15:57.665
Oh, good grief. How do you
expect to live without me?

15:57.748 --> 15:59.750
- [chuckles]
- Jeez.

16:00.834 --> 16:01.919
[sighs]

16:02.002 --> 16:04.004
You're acting really strange again.

16:04.088 --> 16:06.882
Where did you get
this new character this time?

16:08.008 --> 16:09.051
[sighs happily]

16:09.760 --> 16:10.761
It's so peaceful.

16:12.137 --> 16:14.431
You see? It's so nice
when we're not fighting.

16:16.684 --> 16:20.020
What goes through your mind
when things are like this?

16:20.980 --> 16:21.814
Hmm…

16:23.273 --> 16:24.984
I don't really think much.

16:25.651 --> 16:27.736
Just "This is nice." Stuff like that.

16:29.530 --> 16:31.365
Whenever I feel this happy,

16:32.700 --> 16:34.660
I feel anxious as well.

16:35.619 --> 16:36.537
How come?

16:37.454 --> 16:40.457
I get worried that I'll ruin things again.

16:45.254 --> 16:47.881
That won't happen again. Don't worry.

16:51.301 --> 16:52.594
Yeon-su.

16:53.679 --> 16:55.889
[sweet gentle music continues]

16:57.433 --> 16:59.685
Never mind. I'll tell you next time.

17:01.979 --> 17:04.690
[sweet gentle music]

17:05.441 --> 17:06.650
[Yeon-su sighs]

17:11.030 --> 17:13.115
ENROLLMENT GUIDE
SCHOOL OF ARCHITECTURE

17:13.949 --> 17:14.908
[Eun-ho groans]

17:16.577 --> 17:19.663
[sighs, grunts]

17:19.747 --> 17:22.082
Why did you order so much stuff?

17:22.875 --> 17:25.502
But why are there all women's…
Are all these Yeon-su's?

17:25.586 --> 17:27.421
I don't think I ordered that many.

17:27.504 --> 17:30.132
Oh. You're trying so hard
to look like a sweet boyfriend.

17:30.215 --> 17:33.886
Do you really think she'll be happy
when she receives all these things?

17:33.969 --> 17:35.596
She liked it more than I thought.

17:35.679 --> 17:38.348
Too many gifts
will become overwhelming soon, man.

17:38.432 --> 17:40.350
I swear, you can be so clueless, Ung.

17:40.434 --> 17:42.227
I got one for you too.

17:42.311 --> 17:44.438
Where? Which one? What is it?

17:47.858 --> 17:49.234
[Eun-ho] Oh…

17:50.152 --> 17:51.111
This?

17:52.196 --> 17:54.281
It's a bit small
compared to the rest, but…

17:54.907 --> 17:56.366
but thank you.
[chuckles]

17:59.078 --> 18:02.956
Right, Ung. We got the brochure. Ta-da!

18:04.041 --> 18:07.419
Looks nice, huh? It's finally tonight.
Are you ready for that?

18:08.587 --> 18:11.006
We'll be making history
with an exhibition at night.

18:12.049 --> 18:13.425
Is Yeon-su coming today?

18:14.009 --> 18:16.011
- She's coming on the last day.
- Why?

18:16.678 --> 18:18.430
There will be lots of journalists
on the first day,

18:18.514 --> 18:20.974
people might recognize us
because of the documentary.

18:21.058 --> 18:23.977
She said she was okay with it,
but she doesn't want the attention.

18:24.061 --> 18:26.230
Yeon-su is so mature.
She's so thoughtful, too.

18:26.313 --> 18:27.815
[Eun-ho] I wonder what this could be.

18:29.733 --> 18:31.443
[sighs]
You didn't have to, you know.

18:33.487 --> 18:35.114
Why can't I open it?

18:35.197 --> 18:36.240
[box rattles]

18:39.243 --> 18:40.494
- [Ung] Eun-ho.
- Yeah?

18:41.161 --> 18:43.914
I need to tell you something
when the exhibit's over.

18:43.997 --> 18:45.541
What is it? Just tell me now.

18:45.624 --> 18:48.293
No, I can't. After the exhibit ends.

18:48.377 --> 18:51.839
All right.
But why can't I get the tape off?

18:51.922 --> 18:53.006
Do you have long nails?

18:53.090 --> 18:55.551
Can you try
getting this off for me, please?

18:56.677 --> 18:58.929
- What is it, though? Tell me.
- [inhales]

18:59.012 --> 19:01.890
I don't remember.
There was a special sale or something.

19:01.974 --> 19:06.687
Six, five, four, three, two…

19:08.188 --> 19:09.273
[Eun-ho] Sol-i!

19:09.773 --> 19:10.649
[sighs]

19:10.732 --> 19:12.359
What do I do with you?

19:12.442 --> 19:13.569
What are you doing after work?

19:15.487 --> 19:17.739
Why? Why do you wanna know what…

19:19.741 --> 19:21.201
what I'm doing after work?

19:21.285 --> 19:25.080
What? Well, it's Ung's exhibit later.
Come if you're not busy.

19:25.164 --> 19:27.791
We're doing it late at night,
so you can come after work.

19:27.875 --> 19:28.876
Will you be there?

19:28.959 --> 19:30.335
Of course. I'm his manager.

19:31.837 --> 19:33.881
That's right. Of course you are.

19:36.091 --> 19:38.093
[sighs]
You're being so obvious, Eun-ho.

19:38.760 --> 19:39.720
What are you saying?

19:39.803 --> 19:42.014
Are you coming or not?
Do you want a ticket?

19:42.097 --> 19:45.142
Sure, why not. Give me one.

19:48.353 --> 19:49.688
Why are you acting so strange?

19:50.814 --> 19:51.899
You're not sick, are you?

19:53.066 --> 19:55.444
I'm not, why?

19:55.527 --> 19:58.071
Then why, why are you squinting?

20:00.407 --> 20:02.618
Anyway, I should get going, Sol-i.

20:02.701 --> 20:04.786
Oh, and tell me in advance
before you come, okay?

20:04.870 --> 20:06.079
We'll be running for three days.

20:06.788 --> 20:07.915
[Eun-ho] Bye.

20:10.209 --> 20:11.126
Bye.

20:11.919 --> 20:12.920
[Eun-ho] See you.

20:13.462 --> 20:15.839
[cheeky music]

20:17.841 --> 20:19.051
[sighs]

20:19.676 --> 20:22.888
Having a crush is terribly painful.

20:23.472 --> 20:24.973
I know it first hand.

20:28.018 --> 20:29.269
You poor boy.

20:32.439 --> 20:34.024
GO-OH'S EXHIBITION
WHILE THE CITY SLEEPS, OPENS

20:34.107 --> 20:35.150
IT WILL BE A NIGHT-TIME EXHIBIT

20:39.196 --> 20:41.073
- I'm not going.
- What?

20:41.156 --> 20:43.992
What do you mean, you're not going?
Are you bailing on another schedule?

20:44.076 --> 20:45.619
No, of course not. It's not that.

20:45.702 --> 20:47.120
[Chi-seong] Jeez, you startled me.

20:47.204 --> 20:50.040
I'm always so anxious these days
because of you.

20:50.123 --> 20:53.168
Oh, right, you have
the documentary shoot this weekend.

20:53.252 --> 20:54.586
You mean they're still shooting it?

20:54.670 --> 20:56.296
It's already the last episode.

20:56.380 --> 20:57.923
I'll give you the script later.

20:58.006 --> 20:59.675
[engine whirs]

21:01.593 --> 21:03.303
- Chi-seong.
- Hmm?

21:04.888 --> 21:07.849
- I'm sorry.
- What? Why?

21:07.933 --> 21:10.936
About what?
What are you thinking of doing?

21:11.895 --> 21:14.106
No, not something I'm going to do.

21:14.189 --> 21:17.317
I'm apologizing for what I did.
I was acting to rashly.

21:18.360 --> 21:20.237
Couldn't you have
told me that first at least?

21:20.320 --> 21:22.489
You scared me
because you suddenly said sorry.

21:23.156 --> 21:24.449
Well, I won't scare you anymore.

21:26.994 --> 21:30.247
What's gotten into you?
This is making me more nervous.

21:30.831 --> 21:34.251
I'm going to do my very best
to live a normal life now.

21:36.795 --> 21:37.838
Right.

21:38.755 --> 21:40.924
I take back my promise not to scare you.

21:41.008 --> 21:44.803
- I'll scare you a couple more times.
- Can't you just tell me in advance?

21:44.886 --> 21:46.555
So I can take something to calm me down.

21:47.556 --> 21:48.765
[chuckles softly]

21:50.017 --> 21:52.686
[soft music]

22:03.780 --> 22:04.740
[Min-gyeong] Hey.

22:06.116 --> 22:07.159
What are you doing here?

22:08.076 --> 22:08.994
Is Mr. Kim inside?

22:10.329 --> 22:13.749
Isn't he talking about thanking me yet,
for the things I did for him?

22:13.832 --> 22:16.209
He must be grateful
after seeing the viewer ratings.

22:16.293 --> 22:19.504
I don't think he's in the right mind
to do any of that now.

22:19.588 --> 22:22.049
Why? I'm sure he's not busy.

22:22.132 --> 22:24.676
[Min-gyeong] I heard that
he finished all the editing too.

22:28.180 --> 22:30.098
What's going on with him? Did someone die?

22:31.016 --> 22:34.311
I really don't know.
He's not even going home these days.

22:34.394 --> 22:37.439
He acted like that before,
but it seems pretty serious this time.

22:38.315 --> 22:40.025
[sighs]
Look at him.

22:40.942 --> 22:43.195
He's becoming more like Dong-il every day.

22:43.820 --> 22:45.280
You mean Mr. Park?

22:45.363 --> 22:48.617
That's right.
He's acting exactly like him.

22:48.700 --> 22:50.869
Mr. Park isn't the type
to do that, though, I think.

22:50.952 --> 22:52.120
[scoffs]

22:52.204 --> 22:55.874
Don't even get me started.
Because he can be a lot worse.

22:56.374 --> 22:58.960
He could stay all cooped up
in the editing room

22:59.044 --> 23:01.088
whenever something happened.
I'm telling you.

23:02.506 --> 23:04.633
Let's go. Just leave him be.

23:04.716 --> 23:07.844
Why don't we get some coffee?
We should give him some alone time.

23:09.304 --> 23:10.180
Come on.

23:12.808 --> 23:14.142
Come on, let's go.

23:14.226 --> 23:15.352
Oh, okay.

23:20.857 --> 23:22.943
[deep pensive music]

23:23.819 --> 23:25.070
[Ji-ung's mom] I'm dying.

23:25.654 --> 23:26.655
Apparently,

23:27.697 --> 23:29.366
I don't have long to live.

23:30.408 --> 23:31.660
I was wondering…

23:33.161 --> 23:35.038
if you could film me before I die.

23:35.789 --> 23:36.706
Can you?

23:38.125 --> 23:40.502
[deep pensive music continues]

23:51.012 --> 23:53.306
- [Dong-il] Thank you, Chae-ran.
- That coffee is for Ji-ung, though.

23:53.390 --> 23:56.810
Why would you give coffee to someone
who uses up all our electricity?

23:56.893 --> 23:58.728
Don't you feel
the least bit sorry for him?

23:58.812 --> 23:59.771
He's been in there for days.

23:59.855 --> 24:02.315
I feel sorry for myself
for having hired the guy.

24:02.399 --> 24:03.984
[Dong-il] See you. And thanks for this.

24:06.653 --> 24:07.737
[sighs]

24:12.367 --> 24:14.995
Mr. Park is definitely
not the sort of person to do that.

24:15.745 --> 24:19.749
Even if he acts like he doesn't,
he cares about Mr. Kim the most.

24:19.833 --> 24:21.751
Honestly, he cares about him a lot.

24:22.669 --> 24:24.421
I've never seen him care about him.

24:24.504 --> 24:27.007
Do you know why Mr. Kim is still here

24:27.090 --> 24:28.925
when he could have been
an assistant producer?

24:29.009 --> 24:32.554
NEW NOYANGPO FISH MARKET

24:34.931 --> 24:36.141
FIGHT AGAINST FORCED DEMOLITION

24:36.224 --> 24:37.517
WE'RE JOINING THE FIGHT

24:37.601 --> 24:38.602
PROTECT OUR MARKET

24:38.685 --> 24:39.936
THE FISH MARKET IS OUR HOME

24:41.980 --> 24:44.399
Why the hell
did you bring such a useless kid here?

24:44.482 --> 24:45.984
ASSISTANT PRODUCER KIM JI-UNG

24:46.067 --> 24:47.694
[vendors shouting prices]

24:47.777 --> 24:50.280
[shop owner] Do I have to keep working
with this stupid kid?

24:50.363 --> 24:53.283
- Mr. Park! Hey, where the hell are you?
- Yeah?

24:54.993 --> 24:56.161
Hey, what's up?

24:57.704 --> 24:59.956
Hey, come on now,
don't take your anger out on him.

25:00.040 --> 25:01.166
Come on, let's work together.

25:01.249 --> 25:03.418
We've been waiting in line for hours.

25:03.501 --> 25:05.587
He's the assistant producer,
but he's not doing anything.

25:05.670 --> 25:06.922
Are you gonna shoot all night?

25:07.005 --> 25:08.882
Don't you see
we're all working hard over here?

25:08.965 --> 25:11.885
Didn't I tell you I have
to close shop early today!

25:11.968 --> 25:13.845
[shop owner]
It's my wedding anniversary!

25:13.929 --> 25:17.015
I've never been able to go home early
on my anniversaries.

25:17.098 --> 25:20.185
My wife might just divorce me.
Then what? What are you going to do?

25:20.268 --> 25:21.978
Then I'll beg her.
I'll beg her to forgive you.

25:22.062 --> 25:23.813
I swear I will.
Come on, let's take a break.

25:23.897 --> 25:26.483
We should all eat something.
How about it, huh?

25:26.566 --> 25:28.777
Hey, go to the store, will you?
Go buy some ramyeon.

25:29.611 --> 25:32.530
If we had a smarter assistant than him,
we would have ended earlier.

25:32.614 --> 25:35.075
[shop owner] What's the matter with you?
We wasted a whole day!

25:36.534 --> 25:38.995
- Let's go for a smoke. Come on.
- Jeez, man.

25:39.996 --> 25:41.539
[Dong-il] It's all my fault.

25:44.626 --> 25:46.544
[indistinct chatter]

25:53.260 --> 25:54.678
[shop owner] Oh, jeez.

25:54.761 --> 25:57.514
Is this a late-night snack or breakfast?

25:58.139 --> 26:00.600
- Is it done yet?
- Yes, you can eat now.

26:00.684 --> 26:02.602
[Dong-il] Here you go. Here.

26:03.478 --> 26:05.188
- What is this?
- They gave me some.

26:05.272 --> 26:06.690
It's clean, don't worry about it.

26:06.773 --> 26:10.068
You know, you could have gotten us
some crab or maybe even squid instead.

26:10.151 --> 26:12.362
Look at it.
This is going to ruin the taste.

26:12.988 --> 26:15.824
You should have seaweed
on your birthday, you know.

26:16.574 --> 26:17.867
Here you go.

26:17.951 --> 26:19.828
- Is it your birthday?
- Yes.

26:19.911 --> 26:21.788
Hey, now what is all this?

26:21.871 --> 26:25.166
I mean, what kinda lunatic
would put seaweed in ramyeon--

26:25.250 --> 26:26.710
- Just eat it.
- I'll pour it.

26:26.793 --> 26:28.753
It's fine. Let me. Give me your bowl.

26:29.921 --> 26:32.966
Now go ahead and eat up
before it gets cold. Yeah?

26:33.049 --> 26:34.384
Before it gets too soggy.

26:35.218 --> 26:36.344
- Here.
- Eat up.

26:36.428 --> 26:38.596
- [Dong-il] Give me some too.
- Hey, happy birthday.

26:39.306 --> 26:40.181
Eat up.

26:41.933 --> 26:43.059
Thank you.

26:43.810 --> 26:44.811
[Dong-il] Here.

26:44.894 --> 26:46.104
[Min-gyeong] Thank you.

26:46.855 --> 26:48.857
[gentle music]

26:51.901 --> 26:52.861
[Dong-il clears throat]

26:54.029 --> 26:56.823
[Dong-il] They're talking about
the new market that's gonna replace this,

26:56.906 --> 26:59.826
and how there are protests on the news,
that are opposing what's going on.

26:59.909 --> 27:01.536
But look around the market, would you?

27:02.037 --> 27:04.998
People are still
just living their daily normal lives.

27:07.625 --> 27:09.502
Our job is to record things like this.

27:10.253 --> 27:12.505
Things people miss
because it seems so ordinary.

27:12.589 --> 27:15.800
People who live their lives
as mundane and boring as it seems,

27:15.884 --> 27:18.970
and our not so
extraordinary lives as well.

27:19.054 --> 27:22.974
Oh. But if we add them together,
they become stories too.

27:25.018 --> 27:26.686
Don't let him sway you.

27:26.770 --> 27:28.897
You can still go away
while you're still young.

27:29.981 --> 27:34.194
Hey, now try not to mess up, too.
I have to convince him to stay with us!

27:38.239 --> 27:40.033
You're coming tomorrow, right?

27:40.825 --> 27:41.743
[sighs]

27:43.620 --> 27:44.788
Eat up.

27:45.288 --> 27:48.208
- [gentle music]
- [breathes heavily]

27:51.419 --> 27:52.712
[music fades]

27:55.256 --> 27:56.466
What?

27:57.092 --> 27:59.636
Putting seaweed
in a bowl of ramyeon for dinner…

27:59.719 --> 28:01.054
What about it?

28:01.137 --> 28:04.099
Ji-ung did that for me
back when I was an assistant as well.

28:04.182 --> 28:07.811
Hmm?
[laughs]

28:08.603 --> 28:10.230
[Min-gyeong] Did you fall for that?

28:10.313 --> 28:13.858
Oh, Mr. Kim, that sly fox.
He using that to keep you here.

28:14.943 --> 28:16.528
[inhales, sighs]
I knew it.

28:17.112 --> 28:19.280
Your team is much more fun
than the drama team.

28:19.364 --> 28:22.784
WHILE THE CITY SLEEPS
GO-OH SOLO EXHIBIT

28:25.620 --> 28:27.247
EXHIBITION HOURS

28:28.832 --> 28:31.126
[smooth classical music]

28:33.294 --> 28:35.380
[guest chatting in distance]

28:37.048 --> 28:38.216
[sighs]

28:41.219 --> 28:42.512
You can all come in now.

28:42.595 --> 28:43.555
[Eun-ho] Welcome.

28:43.638 --> 28:44.764
Please enjoy the exhibit.

28:44.848 --> 28:46.182
- Thank you for coming.
- [excited chatter]

28:46.266 --> 28:47.517
[Eun-ho] Welcome.

28:47.600 --> 28:48.768
Enjoy the exhibit, okay?

28:50.395 --> 28:51.521
Thank you for coming.

28:55.233 --> 28:57.944
LEADERSHIP TRAINING CO-OP SEMINAR

28:58.027 --> 28:59.404
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION A SUCCESS

28:59.487 --> 29:00.655
You're so cool, Ung.

29:01.656 --> 29:02.490
UNG

29:05.243 --> 29:06.077
Hmm.

29:06.161 --> 29:07.328
Did you get off work?

29:07.412 --> 29:09.372
Mm-hmm, I'm heading home now.

29:09.456 --> 29:12.083
I saw the article.
You look really nice today, too.

29:13.334 --> 29:16.671
Well, there are more people
than I expected. I'm a bit nervous.

29:17.255 --> 29:19.507
You did well during the show
despite the amount of people.

29:19.591 --> 29:21.634
It looks like
you're enjoying the attention.

29:21.718 --> 29:22.594
[Ung sighs]

29:22.677 --> 29:26.055
I just want to finish this quickly
and stay home with you all day.

29:26.139 --> 29:27.348
[Eun-ho] Ung!

29:28.391 --> 29:31.394
Oh. Hey, I should get going.
You're coming on the last day, right?

29:31.478 --> 29:34.022
Mm-hmm. I'll give you
the congratulations out there.

29:35.023 --> 29:37.150
- I miss you, Yeon-su.
- [chuckles]

29:37.233 --> 29:38.359
[Ung] Take care.

29:38.443 --> 29:40.195
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

29:40.278 --> 29:41.863
[breathes heavily]

29:42.572 --> 29:44.449
[reporter] Do you have
regular working hours?

29:44.532 --> 29:45.617
How many hours do you work a day?

29:46.201 --> 29:48.203
It differs depending
on the building's size and shape,

29:48.286 --> 29:50.872
but I work
around 12 hours a day on average.

29:50.955 --> 29:53.875
It's something I can draw
with a lot of detail, so I tend to…

29:53.958 --> 29:56.920
The height I prefer
to draw the most is 35 feet.

29:58.963 --> 30:01.132
["Drawer" continuing]

30:14.729 --> 30:16.981
- [visitor] Congratulations.
- Thank you very much.

30:20.819 --> 30:22.862
- [women] Congratulations.
- This way.

30:23.822 --> 30:25.782
- Welcome.
- [Eun-ho] Welcome.

30:25.865 --> 30:28.076
- [visitors] Thank you!
- I can't believe this.

30:28.618 --> 30:31.287
[woman] You're amazing.
Congratulations. Bye.

30:33.873 --> 30:36.793
["Drawer" continuing]

30:50.139 --> 30:51.349
[sighs]

30:58.398 --> 31:00.358
["Drawer" continuing]

31:13.746 --> 31:17.000
And I think it'd be best if you
check the routes of the customers as well.

31:17.083 --> 31:19.127
- All right.
- Um. Follow me. This way.

31:19.210 --> 31:21.754
This is where they'll be having
the book talk. Right this way.

31:23.798 --> 31:26.050
I think we can hold
the book talk in this room, don't you?

31:26.134 --> 31:27.760
Just send me the seating arrangements.

31:27.844 --> 31:30.763
The writer prefers communicating
with people close up, so I think

31:30.847 --> 31:33.182
- making a circle would be our best option.
- Sure. All right.

31:33.266 --> 31:34.934
And I updated the final arrangements

31:35.018 --> 31:37.729
regarding the filming location
of the drama, so you can share that.

31:37.812 --> 31:38.646
- Okay.
- Okay.

31:38.730 --> 31:40.815
Let's do the seats in a circle.
Let's count how many we need.

31:41.441 --> 31:42.400
[Myeong-ho] You all know

31:42.483 --> 31:44.611
that today's the last day
of Go-oh's exhibit, right?

31:44.694 --> 31:47.906
- [Myeong-ho] So did you all get tickets?
- I went last night with my girlfriend.

31:47.989 --> 31:50.658
- I'm telling you, it was all so nice.
- Really?

31:50.742 --> 31:52.452
- Lucky you.
- [chuckles]

31:53.202 --> 31:55.496
I would have gone too
if I had a girlfriend.

31:55.580 --> 31:58.374
Is Ye-in busy? She probably
doesn't have anyone to go with, right?

31:58.458 --> 32:00.501
Maybe I should go with her.
[chuckles]

32:02.545 --> 32:04.380
[gentle playful music]

32:08.927 --> 32:10.261
I thought you were a ghost!

32:12.513 --> 32:15.058
[gentle playful music continues]

32:17.852 --> 32:18.811
[chuckles softly]

32:26.069 --> 32:28.613
Why… why are you looking at me like that?

32:28.696 --> 32:30.531
[both chuckle awkwardly]

32:30.615 --> 32:33.826
Well, it just that it seems like
you've changed a lot recently.

32:33.910 --> 32:34.953
You seem a bit warmer,

32:35.036 --> 32:37.664
not that you were cold or anything,
I'm just saying in general.

32:37.747 --> 32:39.916
And you even joined us
for the gathering last time.

32:39.999 --> 32:42.502
Looks like you're
in a really good mood these days.

32:42.585 --> 32:44.837
- Doesn't she? She looks really happy.
- Yeah. Right.

32:44.921 --> 32:46.756
- So…
- You're dating someone, right? Is that it?

32:46.839 --> 32:48.007
Tell us, who is it?

32:49.425 --> 32:51.636
- Stop it.
- Um. What are you two trying to say?

32:52.387 --> 32:56.933
Well, I mean, we're just curious
what kind of person changed you into this.

32:57.016 --> 32:59.686
And whether it's somebody
we know at the office or something.

32:59.769 --> 33:02.355
We were wondering
if it's Mr. Jang you're dating.

33:03.231 --> 33:07.485
We just wanted to know
what a cool guy he really is. That's all.

33:08.778 --> 33:11.406
I'm sorry. But that's not for you to know.

33:11.489 --> 33:13.157
Let's keep it professional, okay?

33:13.241 --> 33:14.450
- That's right.
- Yes, of course.

33:14.534 --> 33:17.787
Right then. I'll meet up with the staff,
then we can finish up here.

33:18.413 --> 33:19.497
- All right.
- Yes.

33:21.916 --> 33:23.960
- [Yeon-su] Oh, by the way, Myeong-ho.
- Yes?

33:24.043 --> 33:26.421
- Make sure to come with Ye-in later.
- Where?

33:26.504 --> 33:28.256
To my boyfriend's exhibit.

33:28.339 --> 33:31.217
You'll regret it if you don't come.
It's the last day, isn't it?

33:34.804 --> 33:35.888
Her boyfriend?

33:37.473 --> 33:38.599
Does she mean Go-oh?

33:46.566 --> 33:49.527
Ji-ung. This has to stop.

33:52.155 --> 33:53.489
You want me to stop eating?

33:54.157 --> 33:56.701
[sighs]
That's not what I'm talking about.

33:56.784 --> 33:58.453
So what should I stop, then?

33:58.536 --> 34:00.538
You should stop
going around like a lunatic.

34:04.000 --> 34:05.543
Sit down, my neck hurts.

34:09.172 --> 34:10.715
And seriously, "lunatic"?

34:11.466 --> 34:13.676
Did you really just call me a lunatic?

34:14.260 --> 34:17.180
You know, I was just
going to let you be on your own,

34:17.263 --> 34:18.848
but I think
you're going too far this time.

34:20.308 --> 34:23.019
I know you're having a tough time
with your love life, okay.

34:23.102 --> 34:26.230
But it's not something to brood over
for that long. You're a grown-up.

34:27.648 --> 34:29.984
Oh, yeah. I got rejected too.

34:30.068 --> 34:31.402
And thanks for rubbing it in, Chae-ran.

34:32.278 --> 34:34.030
That really hurts.
[scoffs]

34:36.741 --> 34:39.035
Weren't you acting like this
because of Ms. Kook?

34:39.577 --> 34:42.663
You shouldn't mention her name like that.
I'm heartbroken, right?

34:44.290 --> 34:46.584
Then why aren't you going home yet?

34:47.460 --> 34:49.128
Because I don't want to go home yet.

34:49.712 --> 34:51.464
Well, tell me the reason.

34:51.547 --> 34:52.715
Just because.

34:53.925 --> 34:56.052
- Is there something going on?
- [inhales]

34:56.135 --> 34:57.553
Are you interrogating me?

34:57.637 --> 34:59.931
Mr. Park send you to spy on me?

35:00.014 --> 35:02.141
I'm just really worried about you,
that's all.

35:02.642 --> 35:05.228
I get that you push yourself hard
when you working,

35:05.311 --> 35:06.687
but now you're doing all the work

35:06.771 --> 35:08.397
that you don't even
have to do in the first place.

35:08.481 --> 35:12.235
And besides, you're the one who told me
not to make a habit of working overnight.

35:12.318 --> 35:14.445
So why aren't you going home on time then?

35:18.866 --> 35:20.827
Thanks for worrying about me, Chae-ran.

35:26.124 --> 35:27.500
But don't get so upset.

35:28.376 --> 35:31.420
People are saying you're starting
to act like me. What are you gonna do?

35:33.506 --> 35:35.007
Then you should take care of yourself

35:35.591 --> 35:38.136
so I won't have to worry about you
all the time.

35:38.219 --> 35:39.887
All right, fine.

35:39.971 --> 35:42.473
I can't even work late anymore
because of my juniors nagging.

35:42.557 --> 35:44.559
Hey, look, it's not that--

35:44.642 --> 35:46.894
Just eat your meal. It'll get cold.

35:46.978 --> 35:48.354
[sighs]

35:54.861 --> 35:56.988
[engine whirring]

35:59.073 --> 36:00.116
[sighs]

36:05.705 --> 36:07.039
[phone ringing]

36:08.583 --> 36:09.500
Yes?

36:10.293 --> 36:12.003
Yes. What is it?

36:16.215 --> 36:17.842
[tires screech]

36:17.925 --> 36:20.720
[tense music]

36:27.185 --> 36:28.311
[sighs]

36:29.145 --> 36:31.355
[footsteps approaching]

36:39.071 --> 36:42.283
The way you're looking at me
makes me pretty sad, you know.

36:43.492 --> 36:46.746
Oh, no, I was just startled.
I didn't expect you to come.

36:47.413 --> 36:49.040
- Thank you for coming.
- [chuckles]

36:49.123 --> 36:52.043
Don't be ridiculous.
I got a formal invitation.

36:52.126 --> 36:53.920
You asked me to come, didn't you?

36:56.464 --> 36:59.634
You mean, you didn't send this to me?

37:00.343 --> 37:03.304
Oh, wow. I didn't think
I'd become so pathetic.

37:03.387 --> 37:05.306
Oh, no, I did send it to you.

37:05.389 --> 37:06.807
There. You see?

37:07.391 --> 37:10.061
I was living a busy life,
and I totally forgot about you.

37:10.144 --> 37:12.355
- But I came because you asked me to.
- [chuckles]

37:13.189 --> 37:14.357
It looks like

37:15.107 --> 37:17.193
you were waiting for someone to come, huh?

37:18.110 --> 37:20.321
Oh, I guess she's a bit late.

37:20.947 --> 37:22.406
It's Kook Yeon-su?

37:24.283 --> 37:25.826
And she's still not here?

37:25.910 --> 37:27.745
Your girlfriend's
totally neglecting you, you know.

37:27.828 --> 37:30.081
If you dated me,
this never would've happened…

37:31.415 --> 37:34.460
Hey, that was a joke, all right?
You should smile, I'm kidding.

37:34.543 --> 37:36.003
[both chuckling]

37:37.296 --> 37:41.175
Oh. These flowers, they're really pretty.
Thank you so much.

37:41.259 --> 37:43.010
I'm always the one giving you flowers.

37:43.094 --> 37:45.721
I was used to be
more of a taker than a giver.

37:49.809 --> 37:51.686
Your drawings are still really nice.

37:51.769 --> 37:53.521
Were there a lot of people today?

37:54.105 --> 37:56.941
Oh, well, there were a lot of people
before you came,

37:57.608 --> 38:01.070
but there aren't any at this hour.
Maybe it's too late at night.

38:01.153 --> 38:03.781
Oh, I bought the tickets for this hour.

38:04.949 --> 38:06.033
What?

38:06.826 --> 38:08.703
I bought all the tickets.

38:08.786 --> 38:09.620
What?

38:10.538 --> 38:13.124
They say there are two ways
to make friends with somebody.

38:13.207 --> 38:16.127
Spend a lot of time with them,
or try to make them feel moved.

38:16.210 --> 38:19.505
But making people feel moved
is faster than spending time with them.

38:21.882 --> 38:23.592
[chuckles]
You were touched, weren't you?

38:23.676 --> 38:25.761
Yeah, I know. Well, then…

38:27.346 --> 38:30.141
Let's be friends then.
Real ones this time.

38:31.183 --> 38:34.228
Wow. You are more unusual than I thought.

38:34.312 --> 38:36.397
[inhales]
Someone told me back then,

38:36.981 --> 38:39.233
I can just pretend
to live a normal life if I wanted to.

38:40.026 --> 38:42.194
So I'm going to make friends
like a normal person.

38:42.987 --> 38:45.990
But hey, look,
there's nothing normal about this, though.

38:46.073 --> 38:46.991
Hey, come on…

38:47.825 --> 38:49.952
are you just
going to leave me hanging like this?

38:50.036 --> 38:51.370
Oh, right. Sorry.

38:53.331 --> 38:54.874
[chuckles softly]

38:57.626 --> 38:58.711
[NJ] Do you…

39:00.504 --> 39:02.173
give discounts to friends?

39:02.256 --> 39:04.133
[chuckles]
Of course.

39:07.428 --> 39:10.556
Our editing room ghost is finally leaving!
A round of applause!

39:10.639 --> 39:11.974
Go on, start clapping.

39:13.559 --> 39:15.478
Go home. I hope I never see you again.

39:15.561 --> 39:17.688
I get treated so badly
even if I work so hard.

39:17.772 --> 39:21.567
You don't have to work so hard anymore,
you can just go back home and sleep, okay?

39:21.650 --> 39:23.652
Is your water and electricity
still working? It'll get cut soon.

39:23.736 --> 39:25.363
Oh, give me a break.

39:25.446 --> 39:26.322
[Dong-il] Ji-ung.

39:28.074 --> 39:30.159
How about we get some drinks?
What do you say, huh?

39:30.242 --> 39:32.995
- No thanks.
- I knew it. Get lost.

39:33.079 --> 39:35.498
I'm sick of staying here with you.
I'll just drink with…

39:35.581 --> 39:37.541
Hey, where did he go?

39:37.625 --> 39:38.584
[Ji-ung] Mr. Park.

39:38.667 --> 39:39.835
You should go home too.

39:39.919 --> 39:41.670
It's scary there. Nobody's home.

39:42.671 --> 39:44.298
- All right. Good night.
- Ji-ung.

39:48.761 --> 39:52.139
Is, is there… is there something going on?

39:52.890 --> 39:54.058
There isn't.

40:03.567 --> 40:04.985
[guide] Let's proceed this way.

40:06.362 --> 40:07.863
[visitor] Look, this is fascinating.

40:07.947 --> 40:10.699
Over here you're going to see
some of his recent works.

40:11.784 --> 40:12.827
Ung.

40:13.911 --> 40:16.330
Is Yeon-su still not here?
We have to start closing soon.

40:17.081 --> 40:18.958
- [sighs]
- Should I start wrapping up then?

40:19.625 --> 40:20.960
Okay.

40:21.043 --> 40:22.795
[footsteps receding]

40:24.213 --> 40:25.756
[sighs deeply]

40:37.268 --> 40:38.561
You're so strange, you know?

40:38.644 --> 40:41.063
How could you think
of doing an exhibit at this hour?

40:46.444 --> 40:47.611
I enjoyed your exhibit.

40:48.195 --> 40:49.447
[Nu-a] They're still really good,

40:50.197 --> 40:52.074
but I still don't see any progress.

40:53.409 --> 40:55.161
Is that the reason why you're here?

40:55.244 --> 40:56.996
Just to tell me all that.

40:57.079 --> 40:59.540
- Stop following me around, will you?
- [scoffs]

41:00.624 --> 41:02.251
Did you sell some drawings?

41:02.334 --> 41:04.837
I have no time for you. Just leave.

41:05.337 --> 41:07.715
You can read it on the news
that you love so much.

41:08.424 --> 41:09.717
[sighs]

41:09.800 --> 41:11.093
You're so annoying.

41:15.764 --> 41:18.517
You never mentioned anything
about the plagiarism issue,

41:18.601 --> 41:19.560
if I recall correctly.

41:19.643 --> 41:22.146
Hmm. I'm not interested.

41:25.149 --> 41:26.317
I'll get going then.

41:28.194 --> 41:29.737
What makes you think you're all that?

41:34.533 --> 41:37.495
Do you feel like your life is
all elegant and special

41:37.578 --> 41:39.705
if you just ignore everything around you?

41:39.788 --> 41:40.956
What?

41:43.709 --> 41:45.586
I stole your drawings, Ung.

41:46.921 --> 41:48.964
[charged music]

41:53.385 --> 41:54.470
[teacher] Hey, Tae-seon.

41:55.596 --> 41:58.724
Did you decide what works to hand in?
Are you finished?

41:58.807 --> 41:59.767
Yes, I decided.

42:01.393 --> 42:04.605
- Oh! Hey, this is awesome.
- [chuckles]

42:07.483 --> 42:11.111
Hey. But these seem a bit too similar
to Ung's drawings, don't they?

42:15.824 --> 42:17.284
Really? Uh…

42:20.538 --> 42:22.873
[Nu-a] Hey, Ung.
You think they look like yours too?

42:23.541 --> 42:26.544
Here, let me see yours. Wouldn't it
be bad if they're a bit too similar?

42:29.838 --> 42:31.131
I can draw a new one.

42:31.215 --> 42:34.093
[teacher] What do you mean,
draw a new one? The deadline's tomorrow!

42:34.969 --> 42:36.303
It's fine if I'm late.

42:37.721 --> 42:39.890
[charged music continues]

42:45.563 --> 42:48.399
[Nu-a] What makes you think
you're so special even back then and now?

42:49.733 --> 42:51.318
That's funny, don't you think?

42:51.402 --> 42:53.946
Is that really something
you should be asking me at this point?

42:54.530 --> 42:56.156
There's that face again. See?

42:56.240 --> 42:57.741
It kinda sounds like you're mocking me.

42:58.534 --> 43:00.494
Why? You need more attention?

43:00.578 --> 43:02.871
You pretend
not to be interested in anything.

43:04.999 --> 43:06.083
Yeah, well…

43:07.334 --> 43:10.713
everything must've been easy for you,
since you were born with a silve spoon.

43:10.796 --> 43:14.300
But still, you shouldn't have rubbed it
in other people's faces. Huh.

43:15.134 --> 43:18.137
That kills the spirit of those around you
who are working their butts off.

43:18.220 --> 43:19.430
You know it's really…

43:21.056 --> 43:22.099
It's really annoying.

43:23.392 --> 43:26.604
So then, the best you could do
was copy my drawings?

43:31.275 --> 43:32.651
I was curious

43:32.735 --> 43:35.362
to see how you'd react
after I stole from you.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.240
[Nu-a] But…

43:38.824 --> 43:42.119
you still had that same look on your face,
and when I saw you back then…

43:44.038 --> 43:45.456
I took pity on you.

43:49.168 --> 43:51.253
[vulnerable music]

43:52.630 --> 43:53.714
You what?

43:54.381 --> 43:57.051
[Nu-a] It seemed like
your life was so meaningless

43:57.676 --> 43:59.261
that you abandoned things so easily.

44:01.013 --> 44:04.642
What would your life be,
if you kept living it like that?

44:05.684 --> 44:07.853
[vulnerable music continues]

44:10.689 --> 44:12.441
[Eun-ho] I really can't stand
to hear this.

44:13.275 --> 44:15.361
You don't have any right
to give him any advice.

44:15.444 --> 44:17.696
- You're nothing but a thief.
- [sighs]

44:17.780 --> 44:19.990
I knew it all along. I heard you.

44:20.074 --> 44:22.368
You admitted it yourself
that you plagiarized his work.

44:22.451 --> 44:25.329
All right. I'm going to tell
all the reporters about this.

44:25.412 --> 44:26.705
You just wait and see.

44:28.165 --> 44:30.417
Your drawings all seem pretty boring now.

44:33.545 --> 44:34.755
They're all empty.

44:36.882 --> 44:39.009
[vulnerable music]

44:46.016 --> 44:47.184
[Eun-ho breathes angrily]

44:54.066 --> 44:56.193
[vulnerable music continues]

45:14.795 --> 45:17.005
Hey, what are you still doing here?

45:18.298 --> 45:20.843
You should go see Ung at his exhibit.

45:23.345 --> 45:26.515
Didn't you hear what the doctor
was saying about me earlier?

45:27.099 --> 45:28.892
I'll be just fine.

45:30.477 --> 45:31.478
Now go on.

45:32.271 --> 45:33.856
I'm going to get some sleep.

45:36.817 --> 45:38.068
My goodness.

45:39.027 --> 45:42.656
You get hospitalized
once in a while once you're at this age.

45:42.739 --> 45:45.159
It's no big deal, so go on.

45:46.618 --> 45:47.953
You're doing this on purpose.

45:50.414 --> 45:52.332
Listen, Yeon-su.

45:52.416 --> 45:54.251
You're going to leave me.

45:54.960 --> 45:56.003
You're…

45:58.714 --> 45:59.965
getting ready to leave.

46:01.341 --> 46:02.468
[sighs]

46:03.886 --> 46:05.679
Listen to me carefully, Yeon-su.

46:06.972 --> 46:09.183
You know how tough I can be.

46:09.266 --> 46:11.977
I'm going to live a long, long life.

46:12.644 --> 46:15.189
[Ja-gyeong] Even if the grim reaper
comes to get me,

46:15.272 --> 46:18.066
I'm still going to hold on and stay here.

46:20.694 --> 46:21.945
But then…

46:25.699 --> 46:27.284
I'm just afraid that…

46:28.577 --> 46:30.996
that maybe, just maybe…

46:32.331 --> 46:35.626
I might end up leaving you
all alone some day soon.

46:36.418 --> 46:38.587
Please don't say that, Grandma.

46:39.880 --> 46:41.590
You know, I can't live without you.

46:42.257 --> 46:43.759
[Ja-gyeong] But you should.

46:44.343 --> 46:46.094
You have to live even without me.

46:46.720 --> 46:50.891
You have to eat well and you have to do
everything you want to do.

46:50.974 --> 46:52.351
You have to live on.

46:55.437 --> 46:57.147
But do you know what I think?

46:58.023 --> 47:00.359
You know what I think
whenever I look at you?

47:07.366 --> 47:11.203
You living a life molded after mine,

47:11.912 --> 47:13.789
must be my punishment.

47:15.290 --> 47:16.792
[sighs deeply]

47:17.543 --> 47:20.087
[vulnerable music]

47:20.170 --> 47:21.922
[sniffing]

47:23.090 --> 47:25.259
But all I need is you, Grandma.

47:26.843 --> 47:29.054
And all you need is me, isn't that right?

47:29.137 --> 47:33.058
- And we've lived happily together--
- Yes, all I need is you.

47:33.934 --> 47:38.522
Because all I have left is to grow older.

47:38.605 --> 47:40.941
You're the only one I need, yes.

47:42.067 --> 47:43.443
[Ja-gyeong] But then you…

47:45.028 --> 47:47.906
You shouldn't be
living a life like mine too.

47:50.742 --> 47:53.787
Keep those you care about close to you,

47:54.788 --> 47:57.791
do things that you want to do, live life

47:58.917 --> 48:02.170
and enjoy it,
they way I know you've always wanted to.

48:04.256 --> 48:07.759
You shouldn't live just for me, all right?

48:07.843 --> 48:10.804
[choked sob]

48:11.471 --> 48:13.599
[sobbing]

48:16.935 --> 48:18.895
And so in that way

48:19.646 --> 48:22.941
I won't be ashamed to face
your parents when I go.

48:23.942 --> 48:25.360
[sobbing]

48:30.699 --> 48:33.368
[gentle music]

48:33.452 --> 48:35.370
Oh, my dear.

48:40.334 --> 48:41.793
[music fades]

48:46.089 --> 48:48.842
Oh, hey! Gu Eun-ho!

48:48.925 --> 48:50.469
Hey, Sol-i.

48:50.552 --> 48:51.553
Where are you going?

48:52.888 --> 48:54.348
Ah. Is the exhibit over?

48:54.431 --> 48:56.892
Yeah. Did you just close the bar?

48:56.975 --> 48:58.101
Mm. I did.

48:58.185 --> 48:59.102
Hmm.

48:59.895 --> 49:01.229
What's with the long face?

49:01.813 --> 49:04.399
Shouldn't you be throwing a party
to celebrate ending of the exhibit?

49:04.483 --> 49:06.401
[sighs]
I'm not really in the mood.

49:06.485 --> 49:07.319
[Sol-i] Why?

49:08.695 --> 49:11.198
Hey, where's Ung anyway?
Why are you alone?

49:12.532 --> 49:13.867
[sighs deeply]

49:24.836 --> 49:26.129
[dial tone]

49:31.927 --> 49:34.054
[system] The person you are calling
is unavailable…

49:37.724 --> 49:39.351
[breathes heavily]

49:41.395 --> 49:43.230
[phone buzzing]

49:46.316 --> 49:47.275
Where are you?

49:55.283 --> 49:57.411
[steam hissing]

50:01.415 --> 50:02.958
[plastic rustles]

50:12.884 --> 50:14.970
[both sigh heavily]

50:15.053 --> 50:18.682
I certainly admire your tenacity
in challenging yourself to drink more.

50:18.765 --> 50:20.350
[scoffs]

50:23.019 --> 50:24.396
[chuckles]

50:24.479 --> 50:26.022
Say, this is pretty efficient.

50:26.815 --> 50:28.734
You're already drunk just after this many?

50:29.735 --> 50:31.027
I'm feeling fine.

50:31.611 --> 50:32.821
[chuckles]

50:33.488 --> 50:35.949
You shouldn't have picked up
that kind of drinking habit.

50:37.409 --> 50:38.869
[sighs]

50:42.080 --> 50:43.498
[exhales]

50:46.001 --> 50:48.170
Well, should I match your pace?

50:48.253 --> 50:50.922
I should be able to catch up
if I drink all this.

50:51.840 --> 50:55.135
- Don't act so tough.
- What? You don't believe me?

50:55.218 --> 50:57.137
- I'll show you.
- No, you don't have to.

50:57.220 --> 51:00.098
I didn't call you so you'd get drunk.
Besides, this is mine.

51:01.975 --> 51:03.268
Man, you're so cheap.

51:10.984 --> 51:11.985
[inhales]

51:12.736 --> 51:14.029
[sighs]

51:17.949 --> 51:18.992
Hey.

51:20.869 --> 51:23.747
It's been quite a while
since we drank together like this.

51:26.583 --> 51:27.542
[Ji-ung] Yeah.

51:31.129 --> 51:33.590
My exhibit was until today.
Why didn't you come?

51:36.802 --> 51:38.053
I was busy.

51:38.136 --> 51:40.138
[chuckles]

51:40.222 --> 51:41.431
That's a simple answer.

51:42.390 --> 51:44.893
I'm actually pretty upset with you
if I'm being honest.

51:49.981 --> 51:51.149
What about now?

51:52.108 --> 51:53.443
Are you free now?

51:55.445 --> 51:57.739
I finished all my work until next week.

51:58.323 --> 52:01.993
Look, the people around you will hate you
if you're hogging all the work like that.

52:02.077 --> 52:03.161
Don't you get it?

52:03.245 --> 52:04.412
[scoffs]

52:06.498 --> 52:07.916
[chuckles lightly]

52:10.085 --> 52:11.002
Hey.

52:15.799 --> 52:17.425
My mom's going to die.

52:20.971 --> 52:23.181
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

52:23.265 --> 52:24.724
[humorless chuckle]

52:31.857 --> 52:32.816
[sighs]

52:37.362 --> 52:38.446
But I…

52:41.491 --> 52:43.368
I don't feel the least bit sad.

52:44.661 --> 52:47.831
["Home" continuing]

53:02.012 --> 53:03.513
That's a real pity, huh?

53:05.807 --> 53:06.725
What is?

53:09.895 --> 53:12.439
Just… Everyone.

53:18.403 --> 53:19.487
Us and…

53:21.323 --> 53:22.657
and everyone.

53:24.951 --> 53:28.079
["Home" continuing]

53:48.600 --> 53:50.769
["Home" continuing]

54:05.700 --> 54:07.827
[music fades]

54:07.911 --> 54:09.746
[line trilling]

54:11.164 --> 54:13.333
["Home" continuing]

54:26.346 --> 54:28.348
[indistinct system voice]

54:38.066 --> 54:39.526
[line trilling]

54:40.902 --> 54:42.112
[music fades]

54:54.541 --> 54:55.542
[Dong-il] Excuse me.

54:56.251 --> 54:57.669
Do you need any help?

54:58.545 --> 54:59.546
[sighs]

55:00.547 --> 55:01.881
Are you here to see someone, ma'am?

55:15.311 --> 55:16.312
Hey, Yeon-su!

55:18.356 --> 55:21.192
["The Giving Tree"
by Lee Seung Yoon playing]

55:26.865 --> 55:28.616
What are you doing out here?

55:31.453 --> 55:32.662
I…

55:33.997 --> 55:35.290
I thought I…

55:35.999 --> 55:39.044
ruined everything just like I did before.

55:40.628 --> 55:42.130
What are you talking about?

55:42.213 --> 55:43.965
How long have you been out here?

55:44.966 --> 55:46.259
I just thought that

55:47.343 --> 55:49.387
I ruined everything just like before.

55:50.722 --> 55:52.098
[Yeon-su sobbing softly]

55:52.182 --> 55:53.183
I'm sorry, Ung.

55:54.893 --> 55:56.519
[quivers]
I'm sorry.

55:57.812 --> 55:58.980
I'm sorry.

56:03.902 --> 56:06.696
I told you before. It won't happen.

56:09.240 --> 56:11.826
You're not going to ruin anything.
Don't worry.

56:19.292 --> 56:20.335
Hey, Ung.

56:21.169 --> 56:22.003
Hmm.

56:25.381 --> 56:27.050
I'm in so much pain.

56:28.635 --> 56:31.429
["The Giving Tree" continuing]

56:32.764 --> 56:33.932
[sighs]

56:39.062 --> 56:40.105
[Yeon-su] I…

56:41.356 --> 56:43.358
I can't bear it anymore.

56:49.072 --> 56:49.948
It's all right.

56:50.907 --> 56:52.867
[sobbing]

56:55.870 --> 56:57.747
[sobbing continues]

57:05.755 --> 57:07.257
[Sol-i] Why are you looking so down?

57:09.134 --> 57:10.969
Didn't the exhibit end well earlier?

57:11.553 --> 57:12.679
It was a disaster.

57:12.762 --> 57:13.805
[Sol-i] What?

57:15.098 --> 57:17.433
A famous critic criticized him pretty bad.

57:18.017 --> 57:19.144
Why?

57:19.644 --> 57:21.062
The drawings were so cool, though.

57:22.814 --> 57:24.232
What did they say about him?

57:27.485 --> 57:31.156
Well, Ung is going to need
a lot of comforting today.

57:36.244 --> 57:38.079
HOW LONG WILL GO-OH
STAY TRAPPED IN HIS OWN WORLD?

57:38.163 --> 57:40.874
GO-OH HAS HELD
AN INNOVATIVE NIGHT-TIME EXHIBITION

57:40.957 --> 57:42.834
GO-OH DRAWS DETAILED
ILLUSTRATIONS OF BUILDINGS…

57:42.917 --> 57:47.046
BUT THERE IS IMMATURITY
HIDDEN BEHIND HIS TECHNICAL PROWESS

57:50.800 --> 57:53.553
[Ung] "His drawings
that exhibit his emotions

57:54.512 --> 57:56.139
are similar to the doodles

57:57.140 --> 57:59.267
of a child trapped in his own world."

58:03.438 --> 58:05.565
["The Giving Tree" playing]

58:16.451 --> 58:17.702
Let's go inside.

58:26.127 --> 58:33.134
THREE IDIOTS

